    {
      "_id": "4e99c7a0de14c447",
      "name": "Lore Reference: The Vessel",
      "type": "feat",
      "img": "icons/sundries/documents/document-sealed-red-yellow.webp",
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<h2>The Vessel</h2><p>[ASK] <strong>Lawful category:</strong> construct material without identity, an Exchange category. Bought, receipted, three records. Nobody was ever in it (Insight DC 11: true). <em>\"If she comes back in her own skin, good. This is in case she doesn't.\"</em></p><p><strong>Materials:</strong> burial linen, distilled water, a seed of life, a boundary rune (Quill's), needle and thread, and identity anchors. Prepared like a restoration.</p><p>[EARN] <strong>Why cold-from-inside matters:</strong> Cladis shredded her own thread to get out. What comes back along a mended thread may be only herself: name and mind. Whatever climbs back arrives carrying the palace's cold <em>inside</em> it, and an ordinary body would freeze from the core outward. The grown tissue needs a viable cold adaptation (T4). If her own body makes the crossing, the vessel is simply not used.</p><p><strong>She knows:</strong> the vessel, the restoration materials, what cold does to tissue, that it is for Cladis. <strong>She does not know:</strong> the cold door's timetable, the courier, or the Bridgehollow news beyond rumor.</p>",
          "chat": ""
        },
        "source": {
          "custom": "Varrenmoor DM Guide, Part 7 (Session 14)",
          "book": "",
          "page": "",
          "license": "",
