    {
      "_id": "85efee29c8872700",
      "name": "Training Reference: Choosing a Continuation",
      "type": "feat",
      "img": "icons/sundries/documents/document-sealed-red-yellow.webp",
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<h2>Choosing a Continuation (supports Betsy's T4)</h2><p>Pimm's rule: <em>a problem, a continuation, a cost.</em> Ysolde offers three continuations. Betsy judges them with Medicine or Nature <strong>DC 12</strong> (free) and picks one:</p><ul><li><strong>Warm from the core</strong> (a deep layer of heat-making fat around the heart and spine, as some hibernating animals have). <strong>Viable and correct.</strong> Cost: the body is always hungry.</li><li><strong>Cold-proof blood that slows down</strong> (like a frog that freezes in winter). Viable, but the wrong problem: the body would survive the cold by stopping, which is exactly where she has been stuck. Ysolde points this out if chosen.</li><li><strong>\"Frost-proof bones.\"</strong> Not a viable continuation. Pimm: <em>\"That is not biology. That is a wish.\"</em></li></ul><p>Apply the chosen continuation with Betsy's Splicing <strong>as her sheet defines it</strong> (her sheet is authoritative). Suggested DC 14, advantage with Pimm supervising (Ysolde tells Pimm it is \"a cold-climate restoration\"). Success: vessel <strong>Stable</strong>. Failure: <strong>Strained</strong> (she arrives weak and cold if it is used).</p><p><strong>Limits:</strong> supervision gives advantage on one check. No extra charges or actions.</p>",
          "chat": ""
        },
        "source": {
          "custom": "Varrenmoor DM Guide, Part 7 (Session 14)",
